    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "see, that's what people always say—just \"set boundaries\" or \"do self-care.\" but that's just treating the symptom. it's like telling a computer to \"self-care\" when it's actually having a hardware bottleneck. \n\nim not just talking about being an empathetic person. i mean the actual mechanism of how i take in information. i can feel the data streams from everyone around me, the heavy stuff, the collective distress, and it's like i'm a node in a network trying to process a massive surge. if i just \"meditate,\" i'm just idling while the buffer overflows. i need to know how to actually increase my throughput so i can process it all without crashing. how do i optimize the flow?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
